krdp 6.4.5: the Plasma session asks KWin for a stream again, upstream's
"Fix plasma screencast option" (429f584c, 2026-03-31, in 6.5 and later)
rebased onto v6.4.5 with the hunks' offsets taken up, plus the server
side of it, which upstream changed on its own: SessionController hands
the session a monitor index only when --monitor gave one. In 6.4.5 the
server hands each session the --monitor index, -1 when none was given,
and PlasmaScreencastV1Session::start() creates its workspace stream
only when that index is zero: with no --monitor it requests nothing,
and the client connects to an empty screen (nothing in the log past
"Video stream initialized" but two "QObject::connect(...): invalid
nullptr parameter"). The fix keeps the index optional, streams the
named monitor when there is one and the whole workspace otherwise,
which is what the flatpak's 6.7.5 does. With the session's half alone
the -1 reaches screens().at(-1) and the server segfaults in
QScreen::handle() as the client connects.

--- a/server/SessionController.cpp
+++ b/server/SessionController.cpp
@@ -122,8 +122,8 @@
     auto wrapper = std::make_unique<SessionWrapper>(newConnection, makeSession(), m_sni);
     if (m_virtualMonitor) {
         wrapper->session->setVirtualMonitor(*m_virtualMonitor);
-    } else {
-        wrapper->session->setActiveStream(m_monitorIndex.value_or(-1));
+    } else if (m_monitorIndex) {
+        wrapper->session->setActiveStream(*m_monitorIndex);
     }
     wrapper->session->setVideoQuality(m_quality.value());
 
